        <body>
            <div xml:id="d238">

                <pb facs="0480" n="432" sameAs="frus:frus1877/pg432"/>

                <head>No. 238.<lb/><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Mathews to Mr. Evarts.</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Consulate of the United States of America</hi>,<lb/><hi
                                rendition="#italic">Tangier</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1877-07-28"><hi rendition="#italic">July</hi>
                            28, 1877</date>. (Received August 27.)</dateline>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 245.]</seg></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: I have the honor to inclose the translation
                    of a letter addressed by the Moorish minister of foreign affairs to the foreign
                    representatives, acquainting them that he has received an order from the Sultan
                    to purchase a garden adjoining the Christian cemetery, and to present it to the
                    foreign representatives, considering the want of space in the present one now in
                    use.</p>
                <p>I have, &amp;c.,</p>
                <closer><signed>FELIX A. MATHEWS.</signed></closer>


                <xi:include href="d238-a1.xml" xpointer="d238-a1"/>
            </div>
        </body>
